course: dictionary
lesson: 10732
title: Upload and download
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To upload means to send a file, photo or video from your device to the internet or to another computer. Think of it as sending something away from you. «What you type or upload may be stored by a company you have never met.» Once you upload something, it can end up somewhere you cannot control.
explain: Upload is the opposite of download. Download brings things to your device, and upload sends them away. Upload can also be a noun: an upload is a file that has been uploaded, or the act of uploading.
explain: Stop and think before you upload. «Ask a grown-up before uploading any photo, and never upload ones showing your school badge or home.» Photos and posts can stay online for ever, and strangers might see them.
fact: Upload is a verb: upload, uploads, uploaded, uploading.
fact: Upload can also be a noun: an upload is a file that has been uploaded.
fact: «Upload» means to send a file, photo or video from your device to the internet or to another computer.
fact: «Download» is the opposite of upload: it brings things to your device.
fact: Useful phrases are upload a photo, upload to the cloud and upload speed.
exercise: «Ask a grown-up before uploading any photo.» What does uploading mean here? | Tidying up your desktop | Printing a photo on paper | Hiding a photo in a drawer | *Sending a photo from your device to the internet
exercise: Which word is the opposite of upload? | Share | Print | *Download | Open
exercise: Ms Patel says, «Upload your homework to the class website.» What should you do? | Show your homework to a friend only | Print your homework and hand it in on paper | *Send your homework file to the class website | Delete your homework
test: «What you type or upload may be stored by a company you have never met.» What does this warn you about? | Typing is slower than writing by hand | Companies always delete everything you type | Only grown-ups can see what you type | *Your uploaded things may be kept by people you do not know
test: Which phrase is about how fast a file can be sent to the internet? | Upload to the cloud | Class website | Upload a photo | *Upload speed
exam: Which sentence uses upload correctly as a noun? | We will upload to the cloud tomorrow | Upload the homework to the website | Please upload the photo now | *The class file was an upload from Sam's tablet
